{
  "description": "The authorization flow of a TokenExchangeAuthenticator (default options) after a 401 (lws10-core 'Authorization Server Discovery', 'Protected Resource Metadata' and 'Discovery Validation by a Client'). Replace {A} with the origin of the server under test and {B} with another origin (a test harness with a real loopback server can use http://127.0.0.1:<port> and http://localhost:<port>). The client GETs 'request'; the server answers it 401 with the 'challenge' header fields when it carries no Authorization, and 200 (text/plain 'ok') when it carries 'Authorization: Bearer token-1'. Every GET of a URL in 'documents' gets that response (body: JSON, null for none); anything else not listed is 404. A POST to {A}/as/token (form-encoded) gets 200 {\"access_token\": \"token-1\", \"token_type\": \"Bearer\", \"expires_in\": 300}. expected.outcome is 'ok' (the request is retried once with the token and succeeds), or the error the client raises: 'AuthenticationError' or 'UnauthorizedError'. expected.tokenRequest is the one token request made (its endpoint and its form's resource parameter) or null when none may be made. expected.notFetched lists URLs the client must not request. expected.then lists later GETs, which the server answers 200 'ok' with or without a token, and whether each carries the token.",
  "tokenResponse": { "access_token": "token-1", "token_type": "Bearer", "expires_in": 300 },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "valid",
      "description": "The lws10-core example: the metadata and the storage root are on the requested origin and the metadata names the URL requested. The token is for the storage the Link names, and is sent ahead to URLs inside the storage and its root, and nowhere else.",
      "request": "{A}/storage_1/photos/img.jpg",
      "challenge": {
        "WWW-Authenticate": "Bearer resource_metadata=\"{A}/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/storage_1/photos/img.jpg\", error=\"invalid_token\"",
        "Link": "<{A}/storage_1>; rel=\"https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#storage\""
      },
      "documents": {
        "{A}/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/storage_1/photos/img.jpg": {
          "status": 200,
          "headers": { "content-type": "application/json" },
          "body": { "resource": "{A}/storage_1/photos/img.jpg", "authorization_servers": ["{A}/as"] }
        },
        "{A}/storage_1": {
          "status": 200,
          "headers": { "content-type": "application/lws+cid" },
          "body": {
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/cid/v1", "https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"],
            "id": "{A}/storage_1",
            "type": "Storage",
            "service": [{ "type": "StorageRoot", "serviceEndpoint": "{A}/storage_1/" }]
          }
        },
        "{A}/.well-known/lws-configuration/as": {
          "status": 200,
          "headers": { "content-type": "application/json" },
          "body": {
            "issuer": "{A}/as",
            "token_endpoint": "{A}/as/token",
            "grant_types_supported": ["urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange"],
            "subject_token_types_supported": ["urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt", "urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:id_token", "urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:saml2"]
          }
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "outcome": "ok",
        "tokenRequest": { "endpoint": "{A}/as/token", "resource": "{A}/storage_1" },
        "notFetched": [],
        "then": [
          { "request": "{A}/storage_1/notes/a.txt", "sendsToken": true },
          { "request": "{A}/storage_1", "sendsToken": true },
          { "request": "{A}/storage_10/x", "sendsToken": false },
          { "request": "{B}/storage_1/notes/a.txt", "sendsToken": false }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "request-outside-the-storage-and-its-root",
      "description": "A URL on the storage's origin but outside the storage's path and its root's, such as a service endpoint: it passes the checks, so the retry carries the token; later requests outside the scope get none up front, and their 401 reuses the cached token without a second token request.",
      "request": "{A}/services/inbox",
      "challenge": {
        "WWW-Authenticate": "Bearer resource_metadata=\"{A}/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/services/inbox\", error=\"invalid_token\"",
